            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-45288-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-45288 high vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An attacker may cause an HTTP/2 endpoint to read arbitrary amounts of header data by sending an excessive number of CONTINUATION frames. Maintaining HPACK state requires parsing and processing all HEADERS and CONTINUATION frames on a connection. When a request's headers exceed MaxHeaderBytes, no memory is allocated to store the excess headers, but they are still parsed. This permits an attacker to cause an HTTP/2 endpoint to read arbitrary amounts of header data, all associated with a request which is going to be rejected. These headers can include Huffman-encoded data which is significantly more expensive for the receiver to decode than for an attacker to send. The fix sets a limit on the amount of excess header frames we will process before closing a connection."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-45288\nSeverity: high\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.20.7\nFix Version: 1.21.9,1.22.2\nType: go-module\nLocation: /opt/bitnami/redis-exporter/bin/redis_exporter\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-45288](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-45288)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-45288**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | stdlib  | go1.20.7  | 1.21.9,1.22.2  | go-module  | /opt/bitnami/redis-exporter/bin/redis_exporter  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2023-45288](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-45288)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.20.7"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-50387-libsystemd0",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-50387 high vulnerability for libsystemd0 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Certain DNSSEC aspects of the DNS protocol (in RFC 4033, 4034, 4035, 6840, and related RFCs) allow remote attackers to cause a denial of service (CPU consumption) via one or more DNSSEC responses, aka the \"KeyTrap\" issue. One of the concerns is that, when there is a zone with many DNSKEY and RRSIG records, the protocol specification implies that an algorithm must evaluate all combinations of DNSKEY and RRSIG records."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-50387\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libsystemd0\nVersion: 247.3-7+deb11u4\nFix Version: 247.3-7+deb11u6\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2023-50387](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-50387)",
