            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-50868-libsystemd0",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-50868 high vulnerability for libsystemd0 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The Closest Encloser Proof aspect of the DNS protocol (in RFC 5155 when RFC 9276 guidance is skipped) allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (CPU consumption for SHA-1 computations) via DNSSEC responses in a random subdomain attack, aka the \"NSEC3\" issue. The RFC 5155 specification implies that an algorithm must perform thousands of iterations of a hash function in certain situations."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-50868\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libsystemd0\nVersion: 247.3-7+deb11u4\nFix Version: 247.3-7+deb11u6\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2023-50868](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-50868)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-50868**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libsystemd0  | 247.3-7+deb11u4  | 247.3-7+deb11u6  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2023-50868](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-50868)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
