            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-33601-libc-bin",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-33601 high vulnerability for libc-bin package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "nscd: netgroup cache may terminate daemon on memory allocation failure  The Name Service Cache Daemon's (nscd) netgroup cache uses xmalloc or xrealloc and these functions may terminate the process due to a memory allocation failure resulting in a denial of service to the clients.  The flaw was introduced in glibc 2.15 when the cache was added to nscd.  This vulnerability is only present in the nscd binary."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-33601\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libc-bin\nVersion: 2.31-13+deb11u6\nFix Version: 2.31-13+deb11u10\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2024-33601](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-33601)",
