            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-39326-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-39326 medium vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A malicious HTTP sender can use chunk extensions to cause a receiver reading from a request or response body to read many more bytes from the network than are in the body. A malicious HTTP client can further exploit this to cause a server to automatically read a large amount of data (up to about 1GiB) when a handler fails to read the entire body of a request. Chunk extensions are a little-used HTTP feature which permit including additional metadata in a request or response body sent using the chunked encoding. The net/http chunked encoding reader discards this metadata. A sender can exploit this by inserting a large metadata segment with each byte transferred. The chunk reader now produces an error if the ratio of real body to encoded bytes grows too small."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-39326\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.20.7\nFix Version: 1.20.12,1.21.5\nType: go-module\nLocation: /opt/bitnami/redis-exporter/bin/redis_exporter\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-39326](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-39326)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-39326**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | stdlib  | go1.20.7  | 1.20.12,1.21.5  | go-module  | /opt/bitnami/redis-exporter/bin/redis_exporter  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2023-39326](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-39326)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.20.7"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-32990-libgnutls30",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-32990 high vulnerability for libgnutls30 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A heap-buffer-overflow (off-by-one) flaw was found in the GnuTLS software in the template parsing logic within the certtool utility. When it reads certain settings from a template file, it allows an attacker to cause an out-of-bounds (OOB) NULL pointer write, resulting in memory corruption and a denial-of-service (DoS) that could potentially crash the system."
              },
