              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-4598-libudev1",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-4598 medium vulnerability for libudev1 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A vulnerability was found in systemd-coredump. This flaw allows an attacker to force a SUID process to crash and replace it with a non-SUID binary to access the original's privileged process coredump, allowing the attacker to read sensitive data, such as /etc/shadow content, loaded by the original process.  A SUID binary or process has a special type of permission, which allows the process to run with the file owner's permissions, regardless of the user executing the binary. This allows the process to access more restricted data than unprivileged users or processes would be able to. An attacker can leverage this flaw by forcing a SUID process to crash and force the Linux kernel to recycle the process PID before systemd-coredump can analyze the /proc/pid/auxv file. If the attacker wins the race condition, they gain access to the original's SUID process coredump file. They can read sensitive content loaded into memory by the original binary, affecting data confidentiality."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-4598\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libudev1\nVersion: 247.3-7+deb11u4\nFix Version: 247.3-7+deb11u7\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2025-4598](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-4598)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-4598**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libudev1  | 247.3-7+deb11u4  | 247.3-7+deb11u7  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2025-4598](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-4598)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libudev1@247.3-7%2Bdeb11u4?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-11\u0026upstream=systemd"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-32988-libgnutls30",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-32988 high vulnerability for libgnutls30 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in GnuTLS. A double-free vulnerability exists in GnuTLS due to incorrect ownership handling in the export logic of Subject Alternative Name (SAN) entries containing an otherName. If the type-id OID is invalid or malformed, GnuTLS will call asn1_delete_structure() on an ASN.1 node it does not own, leading to a double-free condition when the parent function or caller later attempts to free the same structure.  This vulnerability can be triggered using only public GnuTLS APIs and may result in denial of service or memory corruption, depending on allocator behavior."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-32988\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libgnutls30\nVersion: 3.7.1-5+deb11u3\nFix Version: 3.7.1-5+deb11u8\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2025-32988](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-32988)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-32988**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libgnutls30  | 3.7.1-5+deb11u3  | 3.7.1-5+deb11u8  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2025-32988](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-32988)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
